# Visual language

Calm, high-end spa: slate neutrals, generous spacing, warm subtle accents (`stone`/`amber` at low saturation). Mobile-first. Avoid harsh contrast, neon, and dense UI.

# Images

Always use `next/image`. Pair with `object-cover` and a descriptive `alt`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<img src="/treatment.jpg" />

// ✅ GOOD
<Image
  src="/treatment.jpg"
  alt="Hot stone massage in a calm treatment room"
  fill
  className="object-cover"
  sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw"
/>
```

# Layout

Start from a single-column padded layout (`px-4`, `py-8`), then add `sm:` / `lg:` columns. Use shadcn/ui primitives before custom controls.
